            "exit_code": 0,
            "stdout_sha256": "44823be8e9ec0a5f55b67afa227f3fae50248a09f5b0190e33bf8c02b7461b18",
            "failure_scenario": "none: the claimed behaviour holds. If rp_ticket_owner accepted an empty owner, a nightly red would open ownerless tickets; the owner-* and missing-owner rows would turn red.",
            "precision_class": "advisory"
          }
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "delta-67ac2e4165-verified",
          "level": "note",
          "message": {
            "text": "The delta 67ac2e4165 is behaviour-preserving. (1) The five printf | grep -q sites became here-strings; a here-string adds the same trailing newline printf '%s\\n' did (the two printf '%s' sites matched a single-line fixed mark), and the reads no longer sit in a pipeline, so no SIGPIPE under pipefail. The own() test in the policy self-test keeps its meaning: it fails the row when rc differs or the chosen text does not match. check_no_pipe_into_grep_q measures 60 against a baseline of 60. (2) LREC and RREC equal the old $LOCAL_HOST$RSUF.json and $REMOTE_HOST$RSUF.json in both modes (plain host names in ladder mode, -gpu in crux mode) and the rm list is the same set. (3) The two re-anchored mutants still bite: the m26 sed now matches the here-string text and is killed by 1 row; crux-ladder-wording and crux-remote-rcpt-name are killed, 35 of 35 in the table. The primary also planted four mutants of its own in a scratch copy (cat of the remote receipt, cp destination, LREC without -gpu, .part name); the table went red on all four."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "scripts/release/models_t1.sh"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 144
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "properties": {
            "grounding": "measured",
            "command": [
              "bash",
              "scripts/check_no_pipe_into_grep_q.sh"
            ],
            "exit_code": 0,
            "stdout_sha256": "7fa401454ffed273a1cbbe649985b88eefc2addf9a0ba828e8a8c0718aa43a77",
            "failure_scenario": "none: the claimed behaviour holds. Had a conversion changed the match input (for example a missing newline for an anchored pattern), a policy self-test or readiness row would have turned red.",
            "precision_class": "advisory"
          }
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "autopilot-repo-variable-defined",
          "level": "note",
          "message": {
            "text": "ap_known_failures uses $REPO, which autopilot.sh never assigns itself. Checked: release_params (lib_release_params.sh, sourced at autopilot.sh:40-41, before any use) sets REPO from RELEASE_REPO. Not a defect."
          },
