      "results": [
        {
          "ruleId": "single-quote-since",
          "level": "warning",
          "message": {
            "text": "release_policy_ladder fails to strip single quotes from `since` version"
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "scripts/lib/release_policy.sh"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 93
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "properties": {
            "grounding": "measured",
            "command": [
              "bash",
              "-c",
              "source scripts/lib/release_policy.sh && cat > test_ladder.yaml <<EOF\n  release_policy:\n    name: crux-smoke\n    since: '0.0.0'\n    date: \"2026-10-07\"\n    quote: \"q\"\n    hosts: [lambda, gx10]\n    thinking: [\"off\", \"on\"]\n    larger_rows: nightly\n    red_row_needs: ticket\n    ticket_owner: \"#123\"\n    release_notes: known_failures\nEOF\nrelease_policy_ladder test_ladder.yaml 1.0.0; echo \"RC=$? WHY=$RP_WHY\""
            ],
            "source": "scripts/lib/release_policy.sh",
            "failure_scenario": "If a user defines `since: '0.0.0'` in the standing release policy, `release_policy_ladder` strips only double quotes. The remaining single quotes cause the version regex match `^[0-9]+\\.[0-9]+\\.[0-9]+$` to fail, causing the policy to erroneously reject the ladder with 'is not X.Y.Z'.",
            "precision_class": "advisory",
            "rationale_for_class": "The antigravity arm is advisory until it has 30 measured samples; the primary reproduced this finding on the reviewed head, which makes it real but does not give the arm blocking authority."
          }
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "single-quote-has-entry",
          "level": "warning",
          "message": {
            "text": "release_policy_has_entry.awk fails to strip single quotes from release versions"
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "scripts/lib/release_policy_has_entry.awk"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 5
