          "properties": {
            "grounding": "measured",
            "command": [
              "bash",
              "-c",
              "cat > test_ladder.yaml <<EOF\n  emergency_scopes:\n    - name: manual-test\n      release: '1.2.3'\nEOF\nawk -v v=\"1.2.3\" -f scripts/lib/release_policy_has_entry.awk test_ladder.yaml; echo \"RC=$?\""
            ],
            "source": "scripts/lib/release_policy_has_entry.awk",
            "failure_scenario": "If a user manually writes `release: '1.2.3'` in an emergency_scopes entry, `gsub(/\"/, \"\", r)` strips only double quotes. The equality check `r == v` fails against `1.2.3`, causing the standing policy to erroneously append a duplicate entry and violate the 'one release takes one ruling' rule.",
            "precision_class": "advisory",
            "rationale_for_class": "The antigravity arm is advisory until it has 30 measured samples; the primary reproduced this finding on the reviewed head, which makes it real but does not give the arm blocking authority."
          }
        },
